{"schema_version":2,"unit_id":"tag:06IU:proof","parent_tag":"06SX","chapter":"formal-defos","node_kind":"proof","risk_level":"R3","source_commit":"a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14","source_text":"If <MATH_0001> is versal then (1) holds by\nLemma <REF_0001>\nand (2) holds by\nRemark <REF_0002>.\nAssume (1) and (2) hold. By\nRemark <REF_0003>\nwe must show that given a diagram in <MATH_0002> as in (2),\nthere exists <MATH_0003> such that\n<MATH_0004>\ncommutes. Let <MATH_0005> be the map guaranteed by (2). Denote\n<MATH_0006> and choose a factorization <MATH_0007>\nlying over <MATH_0008> of the given morphism <MATH_0009>.\nBy (S1) we obtain a commutative diagram\n<MATHSEG_0001>lying over<MATHSEG_0002>\nSet <MATH_0010>. Let <MATH_0011>\nbe the ring map <MATH_0012>,\ncf.<SPACE_0001>Lemma <REF_0004>.\nBy (1) there exists a morphism <MATH_0013> which lies over a ring\nmap <MATH_0014>. Choose an Artinian quotient\n<MATH_0015> such that both <MATH_0016> and <MATH_0017>\nfactor through <MATH_0018>, i.e., giving\n<MATH_0019> and <MATH_0020>.\nChoose a pushforward <MATH_0021>, a factorization\n<MATH_0022> lying over <MATH_0023> of <MATH_0024>, and a\nfactorization <MATH_0025> lying over\n<MATH_0026> of <MATH_0027>.\nApplying (S1) once more we obtain\n<MATHSEG_0003>lying over<MATHSEG_0004>\nNote that the map <MATH_0028> of\nLemma <REF_0005>\n(defined using <MATH_0029>)\nis the composition of <MATH_0030> and the map\n<MATH_0031> above. By construction there exists a morphism\n<MATH_0032>! Hence\nLemma <REF_0006>\napplies (to the outer rectangles in the diagrams above)\nto give a morphism <MATH_0033> and precomposing\nwith <MATH_0034> gives the desired morphism <MATH_0035>.\n","source_status":"CURRENT","placeholders":{"MATH_0001":"$\\xi$","REF_0001":"\\ref{lemma-smooth-morphism-essentially-surjective}","REF_0002":"\\ref{remark-versal-object}","REF_0003":"\\ref{remark-versal-object}","MATH_0002":"$\\widehat{\\mathcal{F}}$","MATH_0003":"$\\xi \\to y$","MATH_0004":"$$\n\\xym